                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is an enhanced version of an old mobile game called Cally's Caves 2.\r\n\r\nThis is a small 2d platformer game that works like old flash games. You play as Cally, who looks like Penny from Inspector Gadget, shooting and jumping over obstacles and pits. There's 6 levels, each one ending with a boss, and a lot of similar looking screens to reach them.\r\n\r\nThe main difference with classic platformers is that you get a shop at the start of each run where you can spend your coins in upgrades, less enemy health, triple jump, etc. It's not a Metroidvania since the required route can be taken without any upgrades, you can even dodge or skip most of the enemies if you are patient enough. Beating a boss will also unlock the ability to buy a direct skip to the next level without having to replay the previous ones again, so combat is encouraged.\r\n\r\nThere are lots of weapons that you find without really exploring, a few are actually needed for destroying blocks in your way and one creates temporary platforms to jump to higher places. All these weapons have a limit of 10 levels where their power grows steady, just shooting an enemy gives you XP for the active one.\r\n\r\nIt's a very simple game and very easy to cheese. You can return to any previous room and everything will reset, including enemies and treasure. I found a specific room in the first world that had lots of crystals very near the entrance, and by spamming this exploit you can get enough cash to buy the entire shop in a relative short amount of time.\r\n\r\nThe game works for what it is, all achievements are related to killing lots of enemies, a little uninspired. Also, if you are wondering where's Cally's Caves 1 or Cally's Trials 1, the developer never rereleased it again because apparently it was too rough, probably for the best.",
